# Line-ending policy for byte-verified artifacts.
#
# Several committed files are checked by SHA256 over their raw bytes, most
# importantly results/runs.jsonl against configs/FROZEN_LEDGER.sha256. Git for
# Windows ships with core.autocrlf=true, which rewrites LF to CRLF on checkout;
# that changes those bytes and the frozen-ledger check then fails. Without this
# file a clean clone on a default Windows install stops at the first build
# stage, reporting the ledger as damaged when nothing is wrong with it.
#
# These paths are therefore exempt from end-of-line translation. Their blobs
# are already stored with LF, so this changes no content -- it only stops Git
# from rewriting them on the way out.
#
# Deliberately narrow: no `* text=auto` rule here. A repository-wide
# normalisation would rewrite every tracked text file on the next commit, which
# is exactly the kind of whole-file diff that hides real changes.

*.jsonl     -text
*.csv       -text
*.sha256    -text

# Compressed and rendered artifacts: never translate, never diff as text.
*.gz        binary
*.pdf       binary
*.png       binary
*.jpeg      binary
*.jpg       binary
